# `import("./named.mjs")` in zero.mjs names the module first, so the start has it evaluated at a time that nobody knows. It suspends, and f.mjs, which imports it by a statement, waits for it as for any other: e.mjs overtakes f.mjs.
# A module that was evaluated "sometime" never said that it waits: f.mjs was followed, `lateOfF` (the one variable of the program's own that holds a text and has a dead zone) lost its dead zone, and `readOfF` counted as laid ahead of every object.
# RUN: link variables mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES: entries-of-bun
# CHECK: proven=string|absent writers-known written-at-construction-alone
# RUN(NEVER): link members mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES(NEVER): entries-of-bun
# NEVER-NOT: "readOfF" {{*}}laid-ahead
# PROGRAM-OF: importer-of-a-member-of-a-cycle-waits-for-the-root-of-the-cycle.ir
